                  %h2#theorems Theorems
                  %ul
                    %li
                      %p
                        %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Diaconescu%27s+theorem"} Diaconescu's theorem
                    %li
                      %p
                        %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Barr%27s+theorem"} Barr's theorem
                  %div
                    %p
                      %a{:href => "/nlab/edit/topos+theory+-+contents"} Edit this sidebar
          %blockquote
            %p
              This page is about
              %strong inverse images of sheaves
              and related subjects. For the set-theoretic operation, see
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/preimage"} preimage
          %hr/
          %h1#inverse_images Inverse images
          .maruku_toc
            %ul
              %li
                %a{:href => "#idea"} Idea
              %li
                %a{:href => "#definition"} Definition
              %ul
                %li
                  %a{:href => "#on_presheaves"} on presheaves
                %li
                  %a{:href => "#on_sheaves"} on sheaves
                %li
                  %a{:href => "#on_sheaves_on_topological_spaces"} on sheaves on topological spaces
              %li
                %a{:href => "#properties"} Properties
              %li
                %a{:href => "#examples"} Examples
              %li
                %a{:href => "#related_concepts"} Related concepts
              %li
                %a{:href => "#references"} References
          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            An
            %em inverse image
            operation is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/left+adjoint"} left adjoint
            part
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi f
                    %mo *
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f^*
            of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometric+morphism"} geometric morphism
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi f
                    %mo *
                  %mo ⊣
                  %msub
                    %mi f
                    %mo *
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi E
                  %mover
                    %munder
                      %mo →
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi f
                          %mo *
                    %mover
                      %mo ←
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi f
                          %mo *
                  %mi F
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (f^* \dashv f_*) \colon E \stackrel{\overset{f^*}{\leftarrow}}{\underset{f_*}{\to}} F
            between
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topoi"} topoi
          %p
            For the case of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sheaf+topoi"} sheaf topoi
            the inverse image
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi f
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mn 1
                  %mo :
                  %mi Sh
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %mi Sh
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  f^{-1} : Sh(Y) \to Sh(X)
          %p
            may be interpreted as encoding the idea of
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pullback+bundle"} pulling back
            along
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
            the “
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bundle"} bundle
            of which the sheaf is the sheaf of sections”.
          %p
            In the case that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y
            are (the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sites"} sites
            corresponding to)
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+spaces"} topological spaces
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/etale+spaces"} etale spaces
          %h2#definition Definition
          %p
            Consider a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functor"} functor
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi f
                    %mi t
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi Y
                  %mo →
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f^t \colon Y \to X
            between the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/underlying"} underlying
            categories of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sites"} sites
          %h3#on_presheaves on presheaves
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/direct+image"} direct image
            operation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi f
                    %mo *
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi PSh
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %mi PSh
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f_* \colon PSh(X) \to PSh(Y)
            on
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/presheaves"} presheaves
            is just precomposition with
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi f
                    %mi t
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f^t
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mi Y
                            %mi op
                        %mtd
                          %mover
                            %mo ⟶
                            %mrow
                              %msub
                                %mi f
                                %mo *
                              %mi F
                        %mtd
                          %mi Set
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                            %mrow
                              %msup
                                %mrow
                                %mrow
                                  %msup
                                    %mi f
                                    %mi t
                          %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} ↓
                        %mtd
                          %mo ↗
                          %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                            %mrow
                              %msub
                                %mo
                                %mi F
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mi X
                            %mi op
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\array{
                  Y^{op}
                  \&amp;\overset{f_* F}{\longrightarrow}&amp;
                  Set
                  \\\
                  \\mathllap{
                  {}^{f^t}
                  }\big\downarrow &amp; \nearrow\mathrlap{_{F}}
                  \\\
                  X^{op}
                  }
                  \\,.
          %p
            The
            %strong inverse image
            operation
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi f
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mn 1
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi PSh
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %mi PSh
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  f^{-1} \colon PSh(Y) \to PSh(X)
          %p
            on
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/presheaves"} presheaves
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/left+adjoint"} left adjoint
            to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/direct+image"} direct image
            operation on presheaves, hence the left
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kan+extension"} Kan extension
            along
            = succeed ":" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi f
                      %mi t
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f^t
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi f
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mn 1
                  %mi F
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo ≔
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %msub
                    %mi Lan
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi f
                        %mi t
                  %mi F
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  f^{-1} F \;\coloneqq\;  Lan_{f^t} F
                  \\,.
          %p .
          %h3#on_sheaves on sheaves
          %p
            The inverse image operation on the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+of+sheaves"} category of sheaves
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Sh
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ⊂
                  %mi PSh
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Sh(Y) \subset PSh(Y)
            inside the category of presheaves involves
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kan+extension"} Kan extension
            followed by
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sheafification"} sheafification
          %p First notice that
          .un_lemma
            %h6#lemma Lemma
            %p
              The
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/direct+image"} direct image
              operation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi f
                      %mo *
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi PSh
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mi PSh
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f_* \colon PSh(X) \to PSh(Y)
              restricts to a functor
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi f
                      %mo *
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi Sh
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mi Sh
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f_* \colon Sh(X) \to Sh(Y)
              that sends sheaves to sheaves.
          .proof
            %h6#proof Proof
            %p
              The direct image
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi f
                      %mo *
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi PSh
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mi PSh
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f_* \colon PSh(X) \to PSh(Y)
              is more generally characterized by
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Hom
                      %mrow
                        %mi PSh
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi Y
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi f
                      %mo *
                    %mi F
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≃
                    %msub
                      %mi Hom
                      %mrow
                        %mi PSh
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi X
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mover
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi f
                          %mi t
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                    %mi A
                    %mo ,
                    %mi F
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    Hom_{PSh(Y)}(A, f_* F)
                    \\simeq
                    Hom_{PSh(X)}(\hat {f^t} A, F)
            %p
              where
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mover
                        %mi f
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                      %mi t
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \hat f^t
              is the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Yoneda+extension"} Yoneda extension
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Y
                    %mo ∘
                    %msup
                      %mi f
                      %mi t
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi Y
                    %mo →
                    %mi PSh
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y \circ f^t \colon Y \to PSh(X)
              to a functor
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mover
                        %mrow
                          %msup
                            %mi f
                            %mi t
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                      %mo :
                      %mi PSh
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi Y
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo →
                      %mi PSh
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \hat {f^t} : PSh(Y) \to PSh(X)
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/co-Yoneda+lemma"} co-Yoneda lemma
              and the colim expression for the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Yoneda+extension"} Yoneda extension
              we have
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable{:columnalign => "right left right left right left right left right left", :columnspacing => "0em", :displaystyle => "true"}
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi Hom
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi A
                            %mo ,
                            %msub
                              %mi f
                              %mo *
                            %mi F
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mo ≃
                            %mi Hom
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %msub
                              %mi colim
                              %mrow
                                %mi Y
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                %mi U
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                                %mo →
                                %mi A
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mi U
                            %mo ,
                            %msub
                              %mi f
                              %mo *
                            %mi F
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo ≃
                            %munder
                              %mi lim
                              %mrow
                                %mi Y
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                %mi U
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                                %mo →
                                %mi A
                            %mi Hom
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi U
                            %mo ,
                            %msub
                              %mi f
                              %mo *
                            %mi F
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo ≃
                            %munder
                              %mi lim
                              %mrow
                                %mi Y
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                %mi U
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                                %mo →
                                %mi A
                            %mi F
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %msup
                              %mi f
                              %mi t
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi U
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo ≃
                            %mi Hom
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %msub
                              %mi colim
                              %mrow
                                %mi Y
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                %mi U
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                                %mo →
                                %mi A
                            %msup
                              %mi f
                              %mi t
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi U
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo ,
                            %mi F
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo ≃
                            %mi Hom
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mover
                              %mrow
                                %msup
                                  %mi f
                                  %mi t
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi A
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo ,
                            %mi F
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                            %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\begin{aligned}
                    Hom(A, f_* F) &amp; \simeq
                    Hom(colim_{Y(U) \to A}) U, f_* F)
                    \\\
                    \&amp; \simeq
                    \\lim_{Y(U) \to A} Hom(U, f_* F)
                    \\\
                    \&amp; \simeq
                    \\lim_{Y(U) \to A} F(f^t(U))
                    \\\
                    \&amp; \simeq
                    Hom( colim_{Y(U) \to A} f^t(U), F )
                    \\\
                    \&amp; \simeq Hom(\hat {f^t}(A), F)
                    \\,.
                    \\end{aligned}
            %p
              Let now
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi π
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi B
                    %mo →
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi \colon B \to A
              be a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/local+isomorphism"} local isomorphism
              in
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi PSh
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi Y
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} PSh(Y)
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sites"} sites
              we have that
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mover
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi f
                          %mi t
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi π
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo :
                    %mover
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi f
                          %mi t
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi B
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mover
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi f
                          %mi t
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\hat {f^t}(\pi) : \hat{f^t}(B) \to \hat{f^t}(A)
            %p
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/local+isomorphism"} local isomorphism
              in
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Hom
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi B
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi f
                      %mo *
                    %mi F
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≃
                    %mi Hom
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mover
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi f
                          %mi t
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi B
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ,
                    %mi F
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mo ≃
                    %mi Hom
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mover
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi f
                          %mi t
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ,
                    %mi F
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≃
                    %mi Hom
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi f
                      %mo *
                    %mi F
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo ,
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    Hom(B, f_* F)
                    \\simeq
                    Hom(\hat {f^t}(B), F)
                    \\stackrel{\simeq}{\to}
                    Hom(\hat {f^t}(A), F)
                    \\simeq
                    Hom(A, f_* F)
                    \\,,
            %p
              where the isomorphism in the middle is due to the fact that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
              is a sheaf on
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi π
                    %mo :
                    %mi B
                    %mo →
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi : B \to A
              in
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi PSh
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi Y
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} PSh(Y)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi f
                      %mo *
                    %mi F
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f_* F
              is a sheaf on
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Y
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y
          .un_defn
            %h6#definition_2 Definition
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo :
                    %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f : X \to Y
              a morphism of
              = succeed "s," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/site"} site
              %strong inverse image of sheaves
              is the functor
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi f
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mn 1
                    %mo :
                    %mi Sh
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mi Sh
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    f^{-1} : Sh(Y) \to Sh(X)
            %p
              defined as the inverse image on presheaves followed by
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sheafification"} sheafification
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi f
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mn 1
                    %mo :
                    %mi Sh
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ↪
                    %mi PSh
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi Lan
                          %mrow
                            %msup
                              %mi f
                              %mi t
                    %mi PSh
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mover
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                    %mi Sh
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    f^{-1} : Sh(Y) \hookrightarrow PSh(Y) \stackrel{Lan_{f^t}}{\to} PSh(X) \stackrel{\bar{-}}{\to}
                    Sh(X)
                    \\,.
          .un_proposition
            %h6#proposition Proposition
            %p
              The inverse image
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi f
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mn 1
                    %mo :
                    %mi Sh
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mi Sh
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f^{-1} : Sh(Y) \to Sh(X)
              of sheaves has the following properties:
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  it is
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/left+adjoint"} left adjoint
                  to the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/direct+image"} direct image
                  = succeed ";" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %msup
                            %mi f
                            %mrow
                              %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                              %mn 1
                          %mo ⊣
                          %msub
                            %mi f
                            %mo *
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (f^{-1} \dashv f_*)
              %li
                %p
                  it therefore commutes with small
                  = succeed "s" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/colimit"} colimit
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/exact+functor"} exact
                  in that it commutes with finite
                  = succeed "s." do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/limit"} limit
          .proof
            %h6#proof_2 Proof
            %p
              The left-adjointness is obtained by the following computation, for any two
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi Sh
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F \in Sh(X)
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi Sh
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G \in Sh(Y)
              and using the above facts as well as the fact that
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sheafification"} sheafification
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mover
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                    %mo :
                    %mi PSh
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mi Sh
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \bar {(-)} : PSh(X) \to Sh(X)
              is
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/left+adjoint"} left adjoint
              to the inclusion
              = succeed ":" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Sh
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ↪
                      %mi PSh
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Sh(X) \hookrightarrow PSh(X)
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable{:columnalign => "right left right left right left right left right left", :columnspacing => "0em", :displaystyle => "true"}
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi Hom
                              %mrow
                                %mi Sh
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                %mi Y
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi G
                            %mo ,
                            %msub
                              %mi f
                              %mo *
                            %mi F
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mo ≃
                            %msub
                              %mi Hom
                              %mrow
                                %mi PSh
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                %mi Y
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi G
                            %mo ,
                            %msub
                              %mi f
                              %mo *
                            %mi F
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo ≃
                            %msub
                              %mi Hom
                              %mrow
                                %mi PSh
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                %mi X
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %msub
                              %mi Lan
                              %mrow
                                %msup
                                  %mi f
                                  %mi t
                            %mi G
                            %mo ,
                            %mi F
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo ≃
                            %msub
                              %mi Hom
                              %mrow
                                %mi Sh
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                %mi X
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mover
                              %mrow
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                %msub
                                  %mi Lan
                                  %mrow
                                    %msup
                                      %mi f
                                      %mi t
                                %mi G
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                            %mo ,
                            %mi F
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo =
                            %mo :
                            %msub
                              %mi Hom
                              %mrow
                                %mi Sh
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                %mi X
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %msup
                              %mi f
                              %mrow
                                %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                                %mn 1
                            %mi G
                            %mo ,
                            %mi F
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\begin{aligned}
                    Hom_{Sh(Y)}(G, f_*F)
                    \&amp; \simeq
                    Hom_{PSh(Y)}(G, f_* F)
                    \\\
                    \&amp; \simeq
                    Hom_{PSh(X)}(Lan_{f^t} G, F)
                    \\\
                    \&amp; \simeq
                    Hom_{Sh(X)}( \bar{(Lan_{f^t} G)}, F)
                    \\\
                    \&amp; =:
                    Hom_{Sh(X)}(f^{-1}G, F)
                    \\end{aligned}
                    \\,.
            %p The proof of left-exactness requires more technology and work.
          %h3#on_sheaves_on_topological_spaces on sheaves on topological spaces
          %p
            In the case where the
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/site"} site
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y
            in question are given by
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+of+open+subsets"} categories of open subsets
            of
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+space"} topological space
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            and
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/etale+space"} etale space
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            and
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mo :
                  %mi X
                  %mo →
                  %mi Y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f : X \to Y
            of the corresponding
            = succeed "s." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/etale+space"} etale space
          %h2#properties Properties
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                See also
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/restriction+and+extension+of+sheaves"} restriction and extension of sheaves
            %li
              %p
                It follows that direct image and inverse image of sheaves define a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometric+morphism"} geometric morphism
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi f
                      %mo :
                      %mi Sh
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo →
                      %mi Sh
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi Y
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f : Sh(X) \to Sh(Y)
                of
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sheaf"} sheaf
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topos"} topoi
            %li
              %p
                Generally, therefore, the left adjoint partner in the adjoint pair defining a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometric+morphism"} geometric morphism
                of
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topos"} topoi
                (or abelian categories of quasicoherent sheaves) is called the
                = succeed "." do
                  %strong inverse image functor
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/noncommutative+geometry"} noncommutative
                morphisms often induce or are defined via pairs of adjoint functors among some associated categories of objects over a geometric space; then the left adjoint part is called the inverse image part. Geometers also often say inverse image for an arbitrary functor of the form
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi f
                        %mo *
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f^*
                in a
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fibered+category"} fibered category
            %li
              %p
                The other adjoint to the
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/direct+image"} direct image
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjoint+functor"} right adjoint
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/restriction+and+extension+of+sheaves"} extension
                of sheaves.
          %h2#examples Examples
          %p
            The standard example is that where
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y
            are
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+space"} topological space
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi S
                      %mi X
                    %mo =
                    %mi Op
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S_X = Op(X)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi S
                    %mi Y
                  %mo =
                  %mi Op
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S_Y = Op(Y)
            are their
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+of+open+subsets"} categories of open subsets.
          %p
            A
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/continuous+map"} continuous map
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mo :
                  %mi X
                  %mo →
                  %mi Y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f : X \to Y
            induces the obvious functor
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi f
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mn 1
                    %mo :
                    %mi Op
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mi Op
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f^{-1} : Op(Y) \to Op(X)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/preimages"} preimages
            of open subsets under continuous maps are open.
          %p Hence presheaves canonically push forward
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi f
                    %mo *
                  %mo :
                  %mi PSh
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %mi PSh
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  f_* : PSh(X) \to PSh(Y)
          %p They do not in the same simple way pull back, since images of open subsets need not be open. The Kan extension computes the best possible approximation:
          %p
            The inverse image
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi f
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mn 1
                  %msup
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo †
                  %mo :
                  %mi PSh
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %mi PSh
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (f^{-1})^\dagger : PSh(Y) \to PSh(X)
            sends
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi F
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi PSh
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F \in PSh(Y)
            to
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi f
                    %mo †
                  %mi F
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi U
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %msub
                    %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} colim
                    %mrow
                      %mi U
                      %mo ⊆
                      %msup
                        %mi f
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                          %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi V
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mi F
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi V
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  f^\dagger F(U) = \colim_{U \subseteq f^{-1}(V)} F(V)
                  \\,.
          %p
            What’s this really doing is using
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi V
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
            to approximate
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi U
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f(U)
            from the outside. Thus a section of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi f
                    %mo †
                  %mi F
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f^\dagger F
            on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi U
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
            will be an equivalence class of sections of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi F
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
            on open neighbourhoods of
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f(U)
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi s
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi V
                    %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ∼
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi t
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi V
                    %mn 2
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "1em"}
                  %munder
                    %mi iff
                    %mo ̲
                  %mspace{:width => "1em"}
                  %mo ∃
                  %mi W
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi Op
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi V
                    %mn 1
                  %mo ∩
                  %msub
                    %mi V
                    %mn 2
                  %mo ⊇
                  %mi W
                  %mo ⊇
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi U
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ,
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi s
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mi W
                  %mo =
                  %mi t
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mi W
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  (s, V_1) \sim (t, V_2) \quad\underline{iff}\quad \exists W \in Op(Y), V_1 \cap V_2 \supseteq W \supseteq f(U), \; s\vert_W = t\vert_W.
          %p
            Compare this with the definition of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/germ"} germs
            at a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stalk"} stalk
          %p
            On the other hand, the extension
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi f
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mn 1
                  %msup
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ‡
                  %mo :
                  %mi PSh
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %mi PSh
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (f^{-1})^\ddagger : PSh(Y) \to PSh(X)
            sends
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi F
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi PSh
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F \in PSh(Y)
            to
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi f
                    %mo ‡
                  %mi F
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi U
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %munder
                    %mi lim
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi f
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                          %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi V
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ⊆
                      %mi U
                  %mi F
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi V
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  f^\ddagger F(U) = \lim_{f^{-1}(V) \subseteq U} F(V)
                  \\,.
          %p
            This approximates the possibly non-open subset
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi U
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f(U)
            by all open subsets
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi V
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
            %em contained
            in it. This corresponds to taking the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kan+extension"} right Kan extension
            instead of the left one, and when it exists it’s called
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/restriction+and+extension+of+sheaves"} extension of presheaves
